You are an expert clinician determining patient eligibility for a clinical trial.

# Patient chart
{chart}

# Trial criteria
{trial}

# Instructions

First, reason step by step. For each inclusion criterion, decide whether the chart establishes it. For each exclusion criterion, decide whether the chart triggers it. Pay special attention to:
- which chart facts are decisive blockers (would, if changed, flip the verdict)
- which chart facts the chart is silent on (deferred to in-person visit)
- which inclusion-supporting facts the patient currently meets (must be preserved)

Output strict JSON only:

{
  "reasoning": "<your step-by-step reasoning, 4-8 sentences>",
  "decisive_blockers": [
    {"side": "inclusion|exclusion", "criterion": "<criterion text>", "chart_fact": "<chart fact making this a blocker>", "would_flip_if_changed": true}
  ],
  "inclusion_supports": [
    {"criterion": "<criterion text>", "chart_fact": "<chart fact establishing this inclusion>"}
  ],
  "deferred_at_visit": [
    {"side": "inclusion|exclusion", "criterion": "<criterion text>"}
  ],
  "eligibility": "eligible" | "ineligible",
  "explanation": "<1-2 sentence summary of why>"
}
